Qualifications and Experience
Candidates should possess a good honours degree (not below Second Class) and a Doctorate in Library and Information Science (this is an academic post of professional ranking. Therefore, it is absolutely necessary for the suitable candidate to hold the PhD degree);
Also, the candidate should have at least fifteen (15) years post-graduate experience, 10 years of which should be in senior management position in the university. Preference would be given to candidates holding the position of Deputy Librarian in a university or comparable institution;
Candidates must also show evidence of considerable scholarship and thorough understanding of the application of new technologies to Library operations and services. Computer literacy and knowledge of the application of ICT in library services are essential requirements;
In addition, candidates must show sufficient evidence of contribution to knowledge through research and scholarly publications in reputable journals within and outside Nigeria. Competence in job planning, organization and ability to take initiatives to fast track the development of a young university library to an international standards within a short period of time.
Applicants for the position of University Librarian must possess the following credentials:
He/she must be a distinguished scholar with exceptional academic and administrative records;
He/she must be a tested and trusted manager of both human and material resources;
He/she must have an in-depth knowledge and understanding of the vision and mission of the university;
d. He/she must be able to attract research grants and complimentary funds from local and international agencies and thereby uplifting the academic status of the university;
He/she must be accountable and should possess the required integrity in the management of resources appropriately;
He/she must demonstrate inter-personal and team building skills;
He/she must be a leader who by his pedigree, is likely to command the respect and loyalty of both staff and students of the university;
He/she should have excellent oral and written communication skills;
He/she should articulate and ensure the enforcement of the university’s laws and regulations;
He/she must be physically and mentally sound;
He/she must be highly proficient in the use of computer and be committed to the development of ICT into the programmes and services of the University;
He/she must not be above fifty-five (55) years of age by October, 2018.
Tenure of Office
The University Librarian shall hold office for a single, non-renewable term of five (5) years.
Salary and Conditions of Service
The successful applicant would be placed on consolidated salary with relevant fringe benefits and would equally enjoy the allowances normally attached to the position of Principal Officers of Nigerian Universities and other benefits as approved by the Governing Council of the University.

